  = note: `shown` is implemented for: i64, (where ((a shown)) (ref a))

error[L0404]: `unit` does not implement `clone`
 --> check/pattern_implementor_errors.rslisp:9:29
  |
9 | (defn clone-units () (clone (make-pair (do) 1)))
  |                             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this needs `clone`
  |
  = note: `clone` is implemented for: bool, char, string, (ref str), i8, i16, i32, i64, i128, isize, u8, u16, u32, u64, u128, usize, f32, f64, (where ((a clone) (b clone)) (pair a b))

error[L0414]: `1` does not fit every type `n` can be
  --> check/pattern_implementor_errors.rslisp:12:19
   |
12 | (defn one (value) 1)
   |                   ^ `n` can be `(ref a)`, which cannot hold this value
   |
   = note: `n` can be any of: i64, (ref a)
   = help: narrow `n` with a trait whose types all hold this value

error[L0404]: `n` might not implement `partial-eq`
  --> check/pattern_implementor_errors.rslisp:15:29
   |
15 | (defn same? (left right) (= left right))
   |                             ^^^^ this needs `partial-eq`
   |
   = help: add the trait to the signature's `where`: `(n partial-eq)`

error[L0418]: a type parameter alone cannot implement a trait
  --> check/pattern_implementor_errors.rslisp:17:37
   |
17 | (rust-trait everything "Everything" (where (a) a))
   |                                     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this would match every type
   |
   = help: wrap the parameter in a type, as in `(where ((a clone)) (ref a))`

